sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, R2-R4, swamp-tasks-model. Nick 2026-11-06: a task VM never holds a GitHub credential; the push step mints its token when it runs, not at admission (an installation token lives one hour). docs/reference/tasks.md#publish-an-external-group.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rule 16 (no tip read: a push without force refuses a divergent tip and pushes nothing for an identical one); rule 22 (no shipped scripts: task VM work is `@swamp/ssh exec` argv, 209 work is inline `git` and `gh api`; one workspace check, since import checks the bundled commit and tree).
  %% Task copy (2026-11-14): a group whose workspace is a task copy exports through its container's workspace phase; the push stays on the worker. The .env Orbit wrote never leaves a copy: the range from the copy's start is checked before the mint. docs/reference/tasks.md#task-copy.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: task:publish
  %% kind: tasks.publish
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Task VM, Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  CLI->>GW: task:publish 42<br/>--check=17
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit task:publish 42 --check=17`
  %%> - syntax: `[task] --check=ID [--title=TEXT --body=TEXT [--draft]] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the task group, and the passed handoff check whose commit is published
  %%> - optionally a title and body together, to open or update the pull request; without them it only pushes
  Note over GW: Check the candidate<br/>task #5165 · record the key names
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - group 42 is an open external group with its own task VM workspace, or with its own task copy whose container runs (`tasks.instance_not_running`) and has a start commit
  %%> - a task copy has no earlier turn that may still run (`tasks.copy_turn_unended`)
  %%> - group 42 is provisioned: while its `tasks.provision` Operation waits or runs, the publish answers `tasks.not_provisioned` (409) with that Operation's ID in `details.operation_id`
  %%> - a task VM runs; a parked VM is woken by the admission, which records its resume, creates no Operation of this kind and answers `tasks.vm_resuming`; repeat the call once the VM runs
  %%> - check 17 passed for group 42, and required hosted CI passed on its commit, else `tasks.commit_not_checked`
  %%> - no other task runs on group 42; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the repository, default branch, commit, checked tree and the task VM's SSH target
  %%> - for a task copy: its Node's SSH target, its container, its start commit and the path of the `.env` Orbit wrote, from the Instance's record
  %%> - names two `task-publish-token-<uuid>` vault keys for the token and the Git authorization header; it mints and writes no value at admission
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5165 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the commit, tree, branch `task-42`, default branch and the optional title and body
  %%> - the vault key names of the token and Git authorization header, never their values; no token exists yet
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5165
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  Note over SW: Create publication scratch
  %%> How:
  %%> - a private worker directory holds the bundle, bare repository and bounded CLI replies
  alt a task copy
    SW->>N: Preflight the copy
    %%> How:
    %%> - the workspace phase reads the checkout as `agent` in the container through its Node; HEAD must be the checked commit
    SW->>N: Export the copy
    %%> How:
    %%> - the workspace phase bundles the branch as `agent`, checks its head and tree against the candidate, and fetches it to this worker; the Node keeps no copy
  else a task VM
    SW->>N: Read the index
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native Git command, with an isolated alternate index on the task VM
    SW->>N: Add workspace files
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native Git command, with an isolated alternate index on the task VM
    SW->>N: Read workspace tree
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native Git command, with an isolated alternate index on the task VM
    SW->>N: Read workspace HEAD
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native Git command, with an isolated alternate index on the task VM
    Note over SW: Check the workspace
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data compares HEAD and the complete tree to the admitted candidate; a mismatch refuses before export
    SW->>N: Export the commit
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
    SW->>N: Copy the bundle
    %%> How:
    %%> - official SSH copy reads the bundle onto the worker; no code is copied to the task VM
  end
  Note over SW: Init the bare repo
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
  Note over SW: Import the bundle
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
  Note over SW: Read bundle contents
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
  Note over SW: Check imported commit
  %%> How:
  %%> - typed data compares the imported commit and tree without a second workspace observation
  opt a task copy
    Note over SW: Check the environment file
    %%> How:
    %%> - every commit from the copy's start to the candidate must hold the `.env` path exactly as the start does; a commit that adds it, even one a later commit removes, refuses with `tasks.publish_secret_path` before any token exists
  end
  SW->>GW: Mint the push token<br/>operation:direct:github-token
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded `curl` step posts the run id to the Gateway when the push is next; the run id proves the caller
  %%> - the Gateway checks the Operation, the run and the repository, mints a token for that one repository with `contents: write`, `pull_requests: write` and `workflows: write`, and writes the two vault values; the reply holds the vault descriptors only
  %%> - a prep run passes its own run id to this step, so the token is minted minutes before the push, not when the prep run was admitted
  %%> - no step writes the token into the task VM; the VM receives no credential, in the bundle, the Git configuration or the environment
  SW->>GH: Push the branch
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded push without force; authorization is a vault-backed extra header in the environment
  Note over SW: Read push result
  %%> How:
  %%> - typed data reads private replies and preserves fast-forward and Workflows refusal codes
  opt --title and --body
    SW->>GH: Read open PRs
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
    Note over SW: Plan the PR
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data selects an open PR or creation and writes unchanged caller prose into a JSON input file
    %%> - with `--draft` the creation carries `draft: true`; an update of an open PR sends only title and body, so a PR keeps its state
    SW->>GH: Write the PR
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded native command on the worker; no shipped script
    Note over SW: Read PR result
    %%> How:
    %%> - typed data keeps only the PR number and URL
  end
  SW->>GH: Revoke the token
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded gh api call, only after a token was minted; a refused revoke is best effort and the token expires within an hour
  alt a task copy
    SW->>N: Discard the copy scratch
    %%> How:
    %%> - the workspace phase removes its guest scratch after failure too, once the preflight passed
  else a task VM
    SW->>N: Remove remote scratch
    %%> How:
    %%> - one bounded SSH argv removes this run's index and bundle after failure too
  end
  Note over SW: Remove local scratch
  %%> How:
  %%> - one bounded command removes the private worker directory and CLI configuration
  Note over SW: Confirm publication
  %%> How:
  %%> - the native assert requires the push, optional PR reply and worker cleanup to be complete
  alt pushed
    GH-->>SW: Branch pushed · head sha
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the branch, commit, and the PR number and URL, or null PR fields for a push alone
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the publication<br/>branch · commit · task done
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a PR receipt makes the group watch its PR and release its VM; a branch-only push keeps its workspace
    %%> - a task copy stays until `task:cancel` or the group's end; its group keeps its status
    %%> - task #5165 succeeds
    opt PR receipt
      GW->>SW: Delete the task VM
      %%> The VM is marked releasing with the publication record. Its deletion removes the workspace, Node, keys and peer; the group holds no task place afterwards.
      SW-->>GW: Confirm deletion
      %%> A later fix turn, build or review round waits for a task place and starts from the base plus the published task branch.
    end
  else a step fails
    GH--xSW: refused or no reply
    %%> When:
    %%> - the workspace moved, the tip diverged, the push or PR write was refused, or a reply was lost
    %%> - a commit of a task copy holds the `.env` Orbit wrote: `tasks.publish_secret_path`; remove that commit from the branch history, then check again
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, such as `tasks.push_failed`
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>group kept · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5165 fails; group 42 and its workspace stay as they are
    %%> On GitHub:
    %%> - a push or PR that started stays; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again: a new task mints a new token at its own push step; an identical tip pushes nothing, and the PR is looked up again before any write
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5165
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
